# Data pipeline

**Three npm scripts** in `packages/data/package.json`: `extract`, `images`, `transform`. The `refresh` script is an alias for `transform --only prices`. Do not add standalone pipeline aliases — use `--only` on these commands during development.

## Run order

```
1. extract  → cache/raw/     (infrequent; cleans cache/scratch/ when done)
2. images   → Blob manifest  (infrequent; cleans cache/images/ when done)
3. transform → cache/normalized/ (frequent; no image downloads)
```

| Command | Folder | Output | When |
| ------- | ------ | ------ | ---- |
| `extract` | `1-extract/` | gitignored `cache/raw/` + `meta/evolution-chains/` | New upstream wiki/API data |
| `images` | `2-images/` | `cache/blob-manifest.json`, deletes `cache/images/` | New/changed sprites, scene art, meta maps/logos |
| `transform` | `3-transform/` | `cache/normalized/` + prices + blogs | Daily (`refresh`) or after extract/images |

`full-sync`: `pnpm extract && pnpm images && pnpm transform`

Meta image filenames are parsed from **raw** Bulbapedia JSON during `images`. Transform applies all Blob CDN URLs in one step: `2-meta/07-apply-manifest-urls.ts` (pokemon `images.json` + meta `imageUrl` / `profileImageUrl` / `logoImageUrl`) after content transforms, before prices/blog.

Extract sources (`--only`): `pokeapi`, `pokemontcg`, `tcgdex`, `bulbapedia-species`, `fandom-species`, `competitive`, `regions`, `generations`, `illustrators`, `expansions`. Meta wiki pairs (`regions`, `illustrators`, `expansions`, `generations`) fetch Bulbapedia then Fandom in one step.

Use `--no-force` to skip unchanged writes on fast pipelines.

### Cache wipe (fresh sync)

Safe to delete and regenerate: `cache/raw/**` (except popularity CSVs), `cache/normalized/**`, `cache/images/**`, `cache/scratch/**`, `cache/extract-manifest.json`.

**Keep (or restore from git):**

| Path | Why |
| ---- | --- |
| `cache/blob-manifest.json` | Image publish checkpoint — avoids re-uploading Blob assets |
| `src/collections/pokemon-collections.json` | Curated collection membership (not built by transform) |
| `cache/raw/popularity/*.csv` | Survey source for meta popularity transform |

`extract` and `transform` call `assertCommittedPipelineInputs()` first. All other cache outputs are rebuilt by the pipeline.

### `images`

**Default:** full incremental pass — sprites, artofpkm, pocket, meta-extract, publish, cleanup. Skips steps already satisfied by `blob-manifest.json` unless `--force`.

```bash
pnpm --filter @repo/data images
pnpm --filter @repo/data images --keep-local   # skip cleanup of cache/images/
```

Legacy alias: `--downloads` (same as default). No separate `meta-images` script.

### `transform` step groups (`--only <group>…`)

```
3-transform/
  1-pokemon/ — pokeapi, bulbapedia, blob URLs, fandom, TCG card flavors,
               cards merge, type profiles, collections, competitive
  2-meta/    — regions, illustrators, expansions, popularity, generations,
               ability descriptions (applies meta Blob URLs from manifest)
  3-prices/  — TCG support caches (incl. pocket URL map from manifest),
               TCGCSV price sync, apply prices, roundups, illustrators
  4-events/  — (reserved)
  5-blog/    — CMS pipeline: facts, card art, per-entity blogs, roundups,
               index, AI polish, coverage verification
```

**`pokemon`** (8 steps): pokeapi, bulbapedia lore, fandom lore, TCG card flavors, cards merge, type profiles, collections, competitive.

**`meta`** (7 steps): Bulbapedia + Fandom regions/illustrators/expansions, popularity, generations, ability descriptions, then **apply-manifest-urls** (single Blob URL write pass).

**`prices`** (5 steps, formerly `refresh`):
1. TCG support caches — promo CDN, trainer-kit URLs, **pocket image map from blob-manifest**
2. TCGCSV price sync — sync bulk index (24h policy; `--allow-frequent-sync` overrides)
3. Apply prices — patch prices into `pokemon/{slug}/cards.json`
4. Expensive by type — roundup snapshots
5. Illustrators — illustrator index + expensive picks

**`blog`** (11 steps): pokemon facts, collect card art, per-species blogs, illustrator blogs, expansion blogs, region blogs, generation blogs, roundup blogs, blog index, AI polish, coverage verification. Derived from accumulated species + meta data — runs last. Output is `cache/normalized/blogs/` which the blog app reads at render time via `packages/data/src/blog/loader.ts`.

```bash
# Run prices group only (daily cron)
pnpm --filter @repo/data transform --only prices
# or
pnpm --filter @repo/data refresh

# Run only blog-derived content
pnpm --filter @repo/data transform --only blog
```

## Layer boundaries

- **Extract** writes raw only — must not read `cache/normalized/`.
- **Images** reads raw + manifest checkpoint; downloads/uploads assets; does not write normalized data.
- **Transform (pokemon)** reads raw + blob manifest; builds normalized species, cards metadata, lore. McDonald's / trainer-kit dupes collapse in `1-pokemon/06-transform-pokemon-cards.ts`.
- **Transform (meta)** reads raw wiki/survey data + blob manifest for CDN URLs; builds region, generation, illustrator, expansion catalogs and popularity index.
- **Transform (prices)** syncs TCGCSV → `cache/raw/tcgcsv/`, patches card prices, rebuilds roundup meta. Card image URLs resolve at **read time** from price-built caches — not persisted per card in core transform.
- **Transform (blog)** derives content from accumulated pokemon data (facts, card art). Runs after pokemon + prices.
- **Runtime prices** are cache-first from the committed TCGCSV index — no per-card live TCGPlayer API on blog requests.

## Timestamps

Run times live **only** in `cache/normalized/meta/pipeline.json` via `writePipelineMeta()`. Never add `extractedAt`, `transformedAt`, `generatedAt`, etc. to per-entity normalized files. See `pipeline-timestamps.mdc`.

## Scripts & temp files

- Shared libs: `packages/data/scripts/lib/` (see `scripts/lib/README.md`).
- Path constants: import from `scripts/lib/paths/cache-paths` → `src/paths.ts`.
- **One-off / debug scripts** → `packages/data/scripts/temp/` (gitignored). Long-lived steps belong in `1-extract/`, `2-images/`, or `3-transform/`.
- Debug a single step: `pnpm exec tsx packages/data/scripts/3-transform/3-prices/02-sync-tcgcsv-prices.ts`

## Common workflows

```bash
# Daily cron (prices only — no image downloads)
pnpm --filter @repo/data refresh

# New TCG sets
pnpm --filter @repo/data extract --only pokemontcg tcgdex
pnpm --filter @repo/data transform

# Annual sprites / scene art / meta maps (infrequent)
pnpm --filter @repo/data extract
pnpm --filter @repo/data images
pnpm --filter @repo/data transform

# Full cache wipe + rebuild
pnpm --filter @repo/data full-sync
```

Long-running loops: see `data-scripts-progress.mdc`.
